From f76ff127b32e241b4afc822d5440e1f39a67b13d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:26:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] runtime(#821): stage every whole-file write through an
 exclusive per-writer temporary [skip ci]

Six more writers staged into one fixed name opened with truncation, the
pattern R-1 found in the generation witness and runtime-config.json:
restart_runtime._atomic_json_write (file-checkpoint profile), the
checkpoint_transactions journal restore, configured_restart._atomic_json_write
(legacy binding file), checkpoint_migration._atomic_json_write,
evaluation.contract.write_run and gauntlet_orchestrator._write_json. On
5ca4bc5b, for every one of them: a writer killed beside another published an
empty file; a symlink at the fixed name was followed; a FIFO there blocked
the writer; a failed rename left the temporary behind.

agentmem_ref/core/atomic_files.py (core layer, standard library only, so
every layer and the evaluation package can use it without importing the
runtime; registered in scripts/restructure_package.py with its alias) creates
.<name>.<pid>.<random>.tmp with O_CREAT|O_EXCL (mode 0o666 less umask, as
before), writes, fsyncs where the writer did, renames, and on any failure
before the rename closes and removes only its own temporary. All seven
writers, runtime-config.json included, now use it; function names,
signatures, bytes written and directory fsyncs are unchanged. The two
evaluation writers keep their no-fsync behaviour.

The Hermes integration's save_config had the same defect at config.tmp, and
its chmod also followed the symlink; it now creates its temporary exclusively
at 0600.

Tests: reference/tests/test_821_fixed_temporaries.py (8, per writer) and
integrations/hermes-agent-memory/tests/test_config_temporary.py (5). The race,
symlink, FIFO and failed-rename tests fail on 5ca4bc5b / e88bced2 and pass
here.

